 <frangarcj@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 22:24:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(textures): shrink glTexSubImage2D orphan copy to
 untouched rows

_glTexSubImage2D orphans (allocates a fresh backing store for) a texture
that was used within the last FRAME_PURGE_FREQ frames, since a scene still
in flight on the GPU may be sampling the current store and vitaGL has no
cheap way to ask GXM whether that scene's fence has signaled yet (short of
sceGxmFinish, a full CPU/GPU stall). That part of the policy is unavoidable
without real per-resource fencing, which would be a much larger change than
this task calls for.

What was avoidable: before applying the caller's update, the orphan path
always memcpy'd the WHOLE old texture into the new store to preserve texels
the update doesn't touch. For a single-level (non-mipmapped) texture, a
full-row update (xoffset == 0, width == full texture width) is about to
overwrite every byte in rows [yoffset, yoffset+height) anyway, so copying
those rows forward first is pure waste - only the rows outside that band
need to survive into the new store.

This is exactly the shape of a row-packed texture atlas/cache that
re-uploads its whole live region (rows [0, yMax)) every frame: the
preserved range now shrinks to the rows above/below the write, down to a
zero-byte copy once the write covers the full height. A 6MB atlas updated
every frame goes from a 6MB copy to whatever fraction is actually unused
this frame. Mipmapped textures and partial-row updates keep the previous
full-copy behavior, since only part of each touched row would otherwise
survive. vglInPlaceTexSubImage still bypasses this whole path as before.
---
 source/textures.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/textures.c b/source/textures.c
index 7c74d7f..3f3c750 100644
--- a/source/textures.c
+++ b/source/textures.c
@@ -981,9 +981,26 @@ static inline __attribute__((always_inline)) void _glTexSubImage2D(texture *tex,
 #endif
 
 #ifndef TEXTURES_SPEEDHACK
-	// Copying the texture in a new mem location and dirtying old one
+	// Orphaning: a scene submitted in the last FRAME_PURGE_FREQ frames may still be in
+	// flight on the GPU and sampling this texture's current backing store, so we cannot
+	// write into it directly (GXM gives us no cheap way to query "has that scene's fence
+	// signaled yet" short of sceGxmFinish, which would stall the CPU on the GPU). Instead
+	// we hand the GPU-visible pointer of the OLD store to sceGxmTextureSetData and rewrite
+	// tex->data to a freshly allocated store, so any in-flight draw keeps sampling the old
+	// (unmodified) memory while we write into the new one; the old store is deferred-freed
+	// via gpu_free_texture_data/mark_as_dirty once FRAME_PURGE_FREQ frames have passed.
+	//
+	// The naive version of this copies the WHOLE old texture forward before applying the
+	// caller's update, to preserve texels the update doesn't touch. But for a single-level
+	// (non-mipmapped) texture, a full-row update (xoffset == 0, width == orig_w) is about to
+	// overwrite every byte in rows [yoffset, yoffset+height) anyway, so forwarding those rows
+	// from the old store is wasted bandwidth: only the rows OUTSIDE that band need to survive.
+	// This is exactly the access pattern of a row-packed texture atlas/cache that re-uploads
+	// its whole live region (e.g. rows [0, yMax)) every frame: the preserved range shrinks to
+	// just the rows above/below the write, down to zero once the write covers the full height.
 	if (!vgl_inplace_texsub && tex->last_frame != OBJ_NOT_USED && (vgl_framecount - tex->last_frame <= FRAME_PURGE_FREQ)) {
 		uint32_t size;
+		GLboolean full_row_update = tex->mip_count <= 1 && xoffset == 0 && (uint32_t)width == orig_w;
 		if (tex->mip_count > 1) {
 			po2_w = nearest_po2(orig_w);
 			po2_h = nearest_po2(orig_h);
@@ -1000,7 +1017,17 @@ static inline __attribute__((always_inline)) void _glTexSubImage2D(texture *tex,
 			size = orig_h * VGL_ALIGN(orig_w, 8) * bpp;
 		}
 		void *texture_data = gpu_alloc_mapped_for_gpu(size);
-		vgl_fast_memcpy(texture_data, tex->data, size);
+		if (full_row_update) {
+			uint32_t stride = VGL_ALIGN(orig_w, 8) * bpp;
+			uint32_t head_size = yoffset * stride;
+			uint32_t tail_off = (yoffset + height) * stride;
+			if (head_size)
+				vgl_fast_memcpy(texture_data, tex->data, head_size);
+			if (tail_off < size)
+				vgl_fast_memcpy((uint8_t *)texture_data + tail_off, (uint8_t *)tex->data + tail_off, size - tail_off);
+		} else {
+			vgl_fast_memcpy(texture_data, tex->data, size);
+		}
 		gpu_free_texture_data(tex);
 		sceGxmTextureSetData(&tex->gxm_tex, texture_data);
 		tex->data = texture_data;
